{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNtcUne4hpzCYVqPmJ8P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `MovementDecoder.toBlock` in `rd-protocol/.../v27/MovementDecoder.java` so negative fixed-point values now truncate toward zero. The rd-protocol tests pass, including new ones for this change.\n\n- **Before:** `Math.round(fixed / 32.0f)` rounded halves up, so a value like -17 (about -0.53 blocks) became -1.\n- **Now:** negatives use integer division, so -17 gives 0, -48 gives -1, and -63 gives -1.\n- **Positives:** these still use `Math.round`, so existing v27 behavior for positive coordinates is unchanged. That fits the project's backwards-compatibility rule.\n- **Callers:** nothing else calls `MovementDecoder`, so no other protocol version is affected.\n\nI read \"round toward zero\" as truncation for negatives only. If you want symmetric truncation, with positives also truncating (48 gives 1 instead of 2), that's a one-line change, but it would alter positive behavior for existing clients. Say if you want it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1488,"cache_read_input_tokens":23433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1488},"output_tokens":350,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c7e22b7-3dad-470e-bceb-dd70bccb5176","uuid":"f1722167-d855-44bd-bc28-319b3202c751","timestamp":"2026-11-25T02:53:41.682Z","request_id":"req_011ChNtcUcUuoaF4ErQ7oT72"}
